From 03ace3644ebfa031a9d4b4744c80b82658967fb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:36:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/57] hw/mchp, hw/arm: reset values checked against PIC32CM
 MC00 silicon

Regenerated after a golden reset dump of a PIC32CM1216MC00048 rev A1
(EV15N46A), every register read after reset-and-halt and compared with
the twin (73 differences before, 19 after, all explained or open):

- DSU ROM table entries carry EPRES; ENTRY1 points at the MTB (the JH01
  ATDF had 0).
- MTB CoreSight identification registers and BASE.
- OSCCTRL.INTFLAG.OSC48MRDY set at reset; PA30 PINCFG.PMUXEN (SWCLK);
  EVSYS.CHSTATUS USRRDY0-11.
- MC00: per-part CAL48M and OSCULP32K calibration, PAC.STATUSC,
  MCLK.AHBMASK 0x7FF, DSU.STATUSC/MEMTYPE, HMATRIX master/slave
  configuration.

The MC00 qtest expects the silicon AHBMASK.

Peripheral Pretender downstream patch; not for upstream submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
